# Project Structure Rules

These rules codify how files and folders **must** be organised in this repository.

---

## 0 — Global

- **Language** — TypeScript only (`.ts`).
- **Imports** — Cross-module imports use the `src/` prefix (e.g., `import { Role } from "src/common/enums"`). Intra-module imports use relative paths (`./`, `../`). Type-only imports use `import type`.
- **File naming** — All source files use **kebab-case** with dot-separated type suffixes (e.g., `create-event.dto.ts`, `event.schema.ts`).
- **Exports** — All entities use **named exports**. No default exports.

---

## 1 — `src/<feature>/` (Feature Modules)

- A **folder = feature module**. Each feature contains:
    - `<feature>.module.ts` — NestJS module declaration
    - `<feature>.controller.ts` — route handlers (HTTP + optional RPC)
    - `<feature>.service.ts` — business logic
    - `<feature>.service.spec.ts` — colocated unit tests
    - `dto/` — `create-<feature>.dto.ts`, `update-<feature>.dto.ts`, and optional sub-object DTOs
    - `schemas/` — Mongoose schema classes
- The controller is a thin dispatcher — **zero business logic**.
- Feature modules do **not** re-declare Mongoose model registrations — models are registered globally in `AppModule`.

---

## 2 — `src/common/`

- Shared enums, types, decorators, and services that span multiple feature modules.
- File naming: `<name>.<type>.ts` (e.g., `enums.ts`, `sqs.service.ts`, `multi-target.dto.ts`).
- Keep this folder flat — no sub-folders.

---

## 3 — `src/filters/`

- Global exception filters registered via `APP_FILTER` in `AppModule`.
- One filter per concern: `http-exception.filter.ts`, `mongo-exception.filter.ts`, `rpc-exception.filter.ts`, `all-exceptions.filter.ts`.
- All filters produce a consistent `ErrorResponse` shape, defined in `error-response.type.ts`.

---

## 4 — `src/strategies/`

- JWT strategy, auth guards, and custom decorators.
- Guards are registered globally via `APP_GUARD` in `AppModule` (order: `ThrottlerGuard` -> `JwtAuthGuard` -> `PermissionsGuard`).
- The `User` type is exported from `jwt.strategy.ts`.

---

## 5 — Root-Level Files

| File                | Purpose                                                                                 |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `main.ts`           | Bootstrap: creates HTTP app, connects TCP microservice, applies global pipes/middleware |
| `app.module.ts`     | Root module: global imports, Mongoose connection, feature modules, global providers     |
| `app.controller.ts` | Health-check endpoint only                                                              |
| `app.service.ts`    | Health-check logic only                                                                 |
| `instruments.ts`    | Sentry SDK initialization (imported at the top of `main.ts`)                            |

---

## 6 — Registrations in `AppModule`

- All Mongoose schemas are registered in `MongooseModule.forFeature` inside `AppModule` (global module).
- All global guards are registered via `APP_GUARD` providers.
- All global exception filters are registered via `APP_FILTER` providers.
- Shared services (e.g., `SqsService`) are declared in `AppModule` providers and listed in `exports`.

---
